{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>לישועתך קויתי ה'. </b>Since our father Jacob saw the might of Samson, he said: even though this one is mighty and victorious, it is not fitting to boast in his might. And so we find that at the time he boasted, he said: ״בלחי החמור הכתי אלף איש״ — and immediately he became very thirsty, until he acknowledged and said: ״ה' אתה נתת ביד עבדך את התשועה״ etc. — acknowledging that there is no might except from HaShem alone. And thus it is said: ״יהי דן נחש עלי דרך״ — and even the might and the victory belong to the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is written: לישועתך קויתי ה'."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The comment blends Judg. 15:15–16 (the donkey's jawbone, a thousand men) with Judg. 15:18 (Samson's thirst) and 16:28 ('you have given...'); all references are implicit in the Hebrew and left unaddressed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:28.367547378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}